---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import tree from "../../data/tree.json";

const API_DEFAULT = "https://api.llms-explorer.com";
const api = String(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_API_URL || API_DEFAULT).replace(/\/+$/, "");
const MAX_INPUT = 4000;

const nodes = tree.nodes;

// The roots and their researched children only. The full browser lives at
// /tree/ — repeating it here would be two things to keep in agreement.
const roots = tree.roots.map((slug) => {
  const node = nodes[slug];
  return {
    slug,
    concept: node.concept,
    children: node.children
      .filter((c) => c.state === "researched" && nodes[c.slug])
      .map((c) => ({ slug: c.slug, concept: c.concept })),
  };
});

// A contributed pack would show up as an artifact hanging off a tree node.
// None do yet, and an empty gallery says so rather than being filled with
// examples nobody submitted.
const contributed = Object.values(nodes)
  .filter((n) => Array.isArray(n.artifacts) && n.artifacts.length > 0)
  .map((n) => ({ slug: n.slug, concept: n.concept, artifacts: n.artifacts }));

const SKILLS = [
  {
    slug: "concept-family-explorer",
    name: "concept-family-explorer",
    role: "Breadth",
    line: "Maps everything around a subject — parent domain, siblings, sub-concepts, adjacent fields, frontier — and finds what is missing from your coverage.",
  },
  {
    slug: "rabbithole",
    name: "rabbithole",
    role: "Depth",
    line: "The narrow inverse: takes one concept and exhausts it — mechanism, edge cases, primary sources, disagreements — until a pass finds nothing new.",
  },
  {
    slug: "llms-concept-abstractor",
    name: "llms-concept-abstractor",
    role: "Extraction",
    line: "Pulls one concept out of a corpus you already hold — the heart from an anatomy textbook, indexing across every database docset — into a concept pack.",
  },
];

const title = "The concept library";
const description =
  `How a concept family gets built — breadth, depth and extraction — over the ${Object.keys(nodes).length} concepts researched so far, with a public library of concept packs anyone can contribute to.`;
---
<Base title={title} description={description} route="/playground/library/" twin={null}>
  <p>
    A concept family is not one skill's output. Three of them build it from
    different directions, and the tree below is what they have produced so far.
  </p>

  <h2>The three directions</h2>
  <dl class="skills">
    {SKILLS.map((s) => (
      <>
        <dt>
          <a href={`/skills/${s.slug}/`}><code>{s.name}</code></a>
          <span class="role">{s.role}</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>{s.line}</dd>
      </>
    ))}
  </dl>
  <p>
    They compose: <code>concept-family-explorer</code> finds the node worth the
    attention, <code>rabbithole</code> exhausts it, and whatever corpus that
    produces is what <code>llms-concept-abstractor</code> reads back. Breadth
    saturates when two rounds turn up no new gaps; depth saturates when two
    passes turn up no new claims. Both stop on evidence rather than on running
    out of ideas.
  </p>

  <h2>The family so far</h2>
  <p>
    {Object.keys(nodes).length} researched concepts under {tree.roots.length} roots,
    generated {tree.generated}. The <a href="/tree/">full tree</a> is browsable and
    filterable; <a href="/tree/3d/">the 3D view</a> is the same graph.
  </p>
  <ul class="tree">
    {roots.map((root) => (
      <li>
        <a href={`/tree/${root.slug}/`}>{root.concept}</a>
        {root.children.length > 0 && (
          <ul>
            {root.children.map((child) => (
              <li><a href={`/tree/${child.slug}/`}>{child.concept}</a></li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        )}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2>Try the extraction step</h2>
  <p class="bounded">
    <strong>A bounded, single-pass demo</strong> of
    <a href="/skills/llms-concept-abstractor/">llms-concept-abstractor</a>: name
    a concept, paste up to {MAX_INPUT} characters of corpus, get a mini concept
    pack. The full skill adds an embedding pass over the whole corpus, several
    lexicon-expansion rounds, and a verification stage — this shows the
    keyword-and-classification core.
  </p>

  <form id="run" data-api={api} data-skill="concept-abstract-mini" data-max={MAX_INPUT}>
    <p>
      <label for="key">API key</label><br />
      <input id="key" type="password" autocomplete="off" size="42" placeholder="llmsx_…" />
      <small>
        Needs the <code>run</code> scope. <a href="/keys/">Create one</a>. Kept
        in this tab only.
      </small>
    </p>
    <p>
      <label for="concept">Concept to abstract</label><br />
      <input id="concept" type="text" size="42" placeholder="indexing, the heart, prompt caching…" />
    </p>
    <p>
      <label for="corpus">Corpus</label>
      <span id="count" aria-live="polite"></span><br />
      <textarea id="corpus" rows="12" cols="80" placeholder="Paste docs, notes, a chapter — anything the concept is buried in."></textarea>
    </p>
    <p>
      <button type="submit" id="go">Abstract it</button>
      <span id="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
    </p>
  </form>

  <div id="result" hidden>
    <h3>Concept pack</h3>
    <p id="cost"><small></small></p>
    <pre id="output"></pre>
  </div>

  <noscript><p>The live demo posts to the API from the browser, so it needs JavaScript.</p></noscript>

  <h2>The public library</h2>
  {contributed.length > 0 ? (
    <ul>
      {contributed.map((c) => (
        <li><a href={`/tree/${c.slug}/`}>{c.concept}</a> — {c.artifacts.length} artifact(s)</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  ) : (
    <p>
      <strong>No contributed packs yet.</strong> Nothing hangs off the public
      tree that came from outside it, so there is nothing to list — be the
      first. This space fills from the tree itself: a pack becomes an artifact
      on the concept it belongs to, and this page reads them back.
    </p>
  )}

  <h3>How contributing actually works</h3>
  <p>
    Contribution is a <strong>merge-back proposal against the public tree</strong>,
    not an upload. You take the tree's current sha, build a patch that adds your
    concept and its artifacts, and submit it to
    <code>POST /api/proposals</code> while signed in — a session, not an API
    key. It goes through a lint gate first: a proposal that fails is still
    recorded, with its findings attached, so an automatic rejection is
    reviewable rather than a dead end. A moderator decides the rest.
  </p>
  <p>
    So the path is: build a pack with the skills above → publish it as your own
    artifact → propose it onto the tree. <a href="/account/">Sign in</a> to
    start; <a href="/reference/concept-tree/">how to read the tree</a> explains
    what a well-formed node looks like before you propose one.
  </p>

  <style>
    .bounded { border-left: 3px solid currentColor; padding-left: .8rem; }
    .skills dt { margin-top: .8rem; font-weight: 600; }
    .skills .role { font-weight: 400; opacity: .7; margin-left: .5rem; font-size: .9em; }
    .tree ul { margin-top: .2rem; }
    #output { white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-x: auto; padding: .8rem; border: 1px solid currentColor; }
    #count.over { font-weight: 700; }
    label { font-weight: 600; }
    small { display: block; }
  </style>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      const form = document.getElementById("run");
      if (!form) return;
      const api = form.dataset.api;
      const skill = form.dataset.skill;
      const max = Number(form.dataset.max);
      const keyField = document.getElementById("key");
      const concept = document.getElementById("concept");
      const corpus = document.getElementById("corpus");
      const count = document.getElementById("count");
      const status = document.getElementById("status");
      const button = document.getElementById("go");
      const result = document.getElementById("result");
      const output = document.getElementById("output");
      const cost = document.getElementById("cost").querySelector("small");

      const STORE = "llmsx.playground.key";
      keyField.value = sessionStorage.getItem(STORE) || "";
      keyField.addEventListener("change", () =>
        sessionStorage.setItem(STORE, keyField.value.trim()));

      const tally = () => {
        const n = corpus.value.length;
        count.textContent = ` — ${n}/${max} characters`;
        count.classList.toggle("over", n > max);
        button.disabled = n === 0 || n > max;
      };
      corpus.addEventListener("input", tally);
      tally();

      form.addEventListener("submit", async (event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        const key = keyField.value.trim();
        if (!key) { status.textContent = " An API key with the run scope is required."; return; }
        if (!concept.value.trim()) { status.textContent = " Name the concept to abstract."; return; }
        button.disabled = true;
        status.textContent = " Running…";
        result.hidden = true;
        try {
          const r = await fetch(`${api}/api/skills/${skill}/run`, {
            method: "POST",
            headers: {
              "content-type": "application/json",
              accept: "application/json",
              authorization: `Bearer ${key}`,
            },
            body: JSON.stringify({ input: corpus.value, concept: concept.value.trim() }),
          });
          const body = await r.json().catch(() => ({}));
          if (!r.ok) {
            status.textContent = ` ${body.detail || `Request failed (${r.status}).`}`;
            if (body.upgrade_url) {
              status.innerHTML += ` <a href="${body.upgrade_url}">Upgrade</a>`;
            }
            return;
          }
          status.textContent = "";
          output.textContent = body.output || "";
          cost.textContent =
            `${body.passes} model pass · ${body.input_tokens} in / ${body.output_tokens} out tokens · ` +
            `job ${body.job_id} · bounded demo of ${body.source_skill}`;
          result.hidden = false;
        } catch (err) {
          status.textContent = " The API could not be reached.";
        } finally {
          button.disabled = false;
          tally();
        }
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
